        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9559025c-32c8-5b4b-9af2-bca3548bfec1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Criss Angel, Christopher Nicholas Sarantakos, Ben Seidman, Marcus Monroe, Luke Jermay\n- Shows and Projects: Criss Angel Mindfreak, Criss Angel Believe, Mindfreak LIVE, The Optical Delusions\n- Organizations and Companies: Cirque du Soleil, A&E\n- Places: Luxor Las Vegas, Las Vegas Strip, Paradise, Nevada, Las Vegas\n- Roles and Topics: magician, illusionist, musician, writer, adviser, tourist revenue\n\nFacts:\n- Christopher Nicholas Sarantakos was born on December 19, 1967, and is known professionally as Criss Angel, an American magician, illusionist, and musician.\n- In 2008, Marcus Monroe, Ben Seidman, and Luke Jermay became founding members of The Optical Delusions, a touring show described as \"an evening of new-school variety.\"\n- In 2010, Criss Angel Believe generated $150 million in tourist revenue for Las Vegas.\n- On May 11, 2016, Mindfreak LIVE replaced Criss Angel Believe, and the new show was partly produced by Cirque du Soleil while Criss Angel retained the directive rights.\n- Criss Angel is known for starring in the television and stage show Criss Angel Mindfreak and for his earlier live illusion show Criss Angel Believe, created in collaboration with Cirque du Soleil at the Luxor casino in Las Vegas.\n- Luxor Las Vegas is a hotel and casino on the southern end of the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, Nevada.\n- Ben Seidman served for three seasons as a writer and adviser on A&E's program Mindfreak starring Criss Angel, and the show used Seidman's inventions.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fc80e3db-d562-5e5f-85fb-1e722b467745",
        "text": "Page: Criss Angel. Sentence: Christopher Nicholas Sarantakos (born December 19, 1967), known by the stage name Criss Angel, is an American magician, illusionist and musician.\nPage: Criss Angel. Sentence: He is known for starring in the television and stage show \"Criss Angel Mindfreak\" and his previous live performance illusion show \"Criss Angel Believe\" in collaboration with \"Cirque du Soleil\" at the Luxor casino in Las Vegas.\nPage: Criss Angel. Sentence: The show generated $150 million in tourist revenue to Las Vegas in 2010, but has since been replaced by \"Mindfreak LIVE\" on 11 May 2016 (the show is partly produced by Cirque, however the directive rights are entirely with Criss Angel).\nPage: Luxor Las Vegas. Sentence: Luxor Las Vegas is a hotel and casino situated on the southern end of the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, Nevada.\nPage: Ben Seidman. Sentence: His inventions are employed in A&E’s program Mindfreak, starring Criss Angel, where Seidman served as writer and adviser for three seasons.\nPage: Marcus Monroe. Sentence: Monroe, along with Ben Seidman and Luke Jermay is a founding member of The Optical Delusions, a 2008 touring show that billed itself as \"an evening of new-school variety.\"",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
